+- 2026-10-14: M21 part 3, dispenser (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +1 test `ticks::tests::a_powered_dispenser_fires_once_after_its_delay`, a layout assert in `craft::tests`). `TileEntityDispenser` is a `Chest` (27 slots, the first 9 used) in `App::chests`, so it is saved, spilled when the block goes (`gone` now accepts block 23) and shared with the chest code; `chest::usable` accepts it too. Screen: `Screen::at_dispenser` has `gw` 9 (a chest screen is always 27 n), `craft::layout(9)` = `ContainerDispenser` (3 x 3 at (62, 17), the inventory as in the workbench), `panel_size` 166 high, `ext` / `with_ext` take 9 slots, label "Dispenser". Firing: `neighbour` (a power source changed, powered here or above) schedules 4 ticks, `update` pushes `Ticks::dispenses`, `App::dispense` = `dispenseItem` (random filled slot with chance 1 / n each, one item out the front; arrow, egg, snowball fly at 1.1 with spread 6 through `Mobs::shoot`, the rest drops with `Drops::throw_from`). Facing from the yaw (`pick::facing_meta` 23 = the furnace table), the front tile follows the metadata. ponytail: no click or shoot sounds, no smoke particles, an empty dispenser does nothing.
 - 2026-10-14: M21 part 2: repeater, note block, jukebox, redstone recipes (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +1 test `ticks::tests::repeater_delays_and_passes_the_signal_on`, 3 lines in `craft::tests::plain_recipes_match_java`). Repeater: `redstone::repeater_input` = `func_22022_g`, `weak` / `strong` of an active one point out of its front only, `ticks` schedules a change after `(delay + 1) * 2` game ticks (`updateTick`, `onNeighborBlockChange`), right click cycles the delay, placement takes the yaw (`pick::facing_meta` 93) and schedules at once when powered; it drops item 356. The wire now looks at its neighbours along Java directions (`isPowerProviderOrWire` with `dir`: a repeater only along its axis, a neighbour one step up or down only if it is another wire; FIX part 1 let any power source connect diagonally). Drawn as a 2/16 box + two torches (`renderBlockRedstoneRepeater` offsets). Note block: `Ticks::notes` (note, last power) + `note_events` (cell, note, instrument), right click raises the pitch, power turns it on (`BlockNote`); nothing plays (no audio layer) and the notes are not saved. Jukebox: the record lives in the block metadata (1 = 13, 2 = cat; the Java uses a tile entity), right click inserts / ejects, breaking ejects. Recipes: `CraftingManager` lines 27 / 28 / 68-79. ponytail: the repeater has no collision box, no particles.
 - 2026-10-14: M20 finished except maps (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run). (1) Compass and clock: `Anim::gauges` ports `TextureCompassFX` (needle chasing the world spawn, red tip, grey tail) and `TextureWatchFX` (the dial turned into the magenta face by the sky angle); the spring is shared (`chase`); written every 20 Hz tick into the atlas (`ChunkPipeline::animate_items`, mips too) and into the HUD's copy of items.png (`HudPipeline::animate_items`); `assets/dial.rgba` (`misc/dial.png`, 1024 bytes, written by `tools/gen_terrain.py`) is new and must exist. (2) Wolves: `gear::befriend` = `EntityWolf.interact` (bone: 1 in 3 tames, health 20, sits, 7 hearts, else 7 smoke; pork heals 3; a tap on a tame wolf toggles sitting) and `ItemSaddle` / `EntityPig.interact` (saddle on a pig, then a tap mounts); a sitting wolf stays, a tame one follows beyond 5 blocks and is put beside the owner beyond 16, never despawns, is not angered by its owner; `Fx::Heart` = `EntityHeartFX`. (3) Riding: `Mob::ridden`, the player's body sits 0.175 over the pig's feet (`updateRiderPosition`), no fall damage, jump = get off (touch has no sneak); the pig keeps its own AI (b1.7.3 has no steering). (4) `world/path.rs`: `Pathfinder` (A*, 4-connected, one step up, drops of up to 3, no water or lava, mob size boxes) used by `Mob::chase` for a target and for a following wolf (repath 1 in 20, jump when the next point is higher); wandering stays a straight walk. ponytail: heap with lazy deletion (ties may differ), 3000 expansions, the wolf teleports beyond 16 instead of when no path is found, no collar colour, no shaking, tame wolves do not fight, the camera does not turn with the pig.
 - 2026-10-14: FIX jagged edges on every line (outline, block edges, plants) (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; `post::tests::shader_validates_in_every_configuration` now also validates `Settings::legacy()`, not run): the legacy frame had no anti-aliasing at all (TAA, FXAA, CAS off) and renders at `RENDER_SCALE` 0.67, so every edge was a stair-step. `Settings::legacy()` turns on the pack's FXAA (`c21_fxaa`, already ported; one full-screen pass at scene resolution, before the upscale).
